    {
      "title": "File:PlayStation 3 Wireless Keypad - Close Up.jpg",
      "pageid": 8749753,
      "sourcePage": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PlayStation_3_Wireless_Keypad_-_Close_Up.jpg",
      "original": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8c/PlayStation_3_Wireless_Keypad_-_Close_Up.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original",
      "thumbnail": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/PlayStation_3_Wireless_Keypad_-_Close_Up.jpg/960px-PlayStation_3_Wireless_Keypad_-_Close_Up.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail",
      "metadata": {
        "DateTime": {
          "value": "2009-12-15 00:17:11",
          "source": "mediawiki-metadata",
          "hidden": ""
        },
        "ObjectName": {
          "value": "PlayStation 3 Wireless Keypad - Close Up",
          "source": "mediawiki-metadata"
        },
        "CommonsMetadataExtension": {
          "value": 1.2,
          "source": "extension",
          "hidden": ""
        },
        "Categories": {
          "value": "Taken with Canon EOS 400D|PlayStation 3 Wireless Keypad|Flickr images reviewed by File Upload Bot (Magnus Manske)|English QWERTY keyboard layouts|Photographs by William Hook",
          "source": "commons-categories",
          "hidden": ""
        },
        "Assessments": {
          "value": "",
          "source": "commons-categories",
          "hidden": ""
        },
        "ImageDescription": {
          "value": "<p>The new PlayStation 3 Wireless Keypad. Arrived today, from Game. :D\n</p><p>The overall weight is still pretty light, even with this attatched - it's about the same as an Xbox 360 wireless controller weighs.\n</p><p>While you're browsing the web, if you hit the middle button (the one with the finger on it) below the Sony logo, the Qwerty part turns into a trackpad. However, it's horrible at this, as the pointer jumps around like crazy. It's fine as a keyboard though.\n</p>\nOverall, it's pretty good - slightly weird though, for one, it would have been nice to not need to switch it on and off manually (even though it does go off automaticially after a while), and secondly, it has its own USB port - so now, once the batteries are flat, you have to charge the controller, then the keyboard. I'd need three USB cables to charge all three at once now - two controllers and the keypad.",
          "source": "commons-desc-page"
        },
        "DateTimeOriginal": {
          "value": "2008-12-04 10:44",
          "source": "commons-desc-page"
        },
        "Credit": {
          "value": "<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/83542829@N00/3081481157/\">PlayStation 3 Wireless Keypad - Close Up</a>\n</p>\n<ul><li>Uploaded by <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=User:Mewtu&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"User:Mewtu (page does not exist)\">Mewtu</a></li></ul>",
